## SECTION (a) — THE RIDER (lines 3809–3843): its three claims, verified independently
================================================================================

CLAIM A1 — the compatible choice B0 = −L_κ(ση^{q(κ)}) is (LIFT)-permitted.

  Byte-read of the recipe. HE6_PROOF_2026-08-08.md, DEFINITION HE6-1, lines 201–205
  (span HE6-FAMILY = 201–213; each line verified `grep -cFx` = 1):

    201 `> **DEFINITION HE6-1 (THE ENLARGED TEST FAMILY).** Let κ = u/ℓ ∈ ℚ in lowest`
    202 `> terms with κ > D′h, and let r = Z^{d} + Σ_{t<d}c_tZ^t ∈ K[Z] be monic`
    203 `> irreducible with r(0) ≠ 0. Choose, by (LIFT), B_t ∈ O[x] with`
    204 `> deg B_t < D′, dv(B_t) = (d−t)u and res(B_t(θ)/ϖ(θ)^{(d−t)u}) = c_t (and`
    205 `> B_t := 0 if c_t = 0), and set`

  At (ℓ,d) = (1,1): u = ℓκ = κ, t = 0, so (d−t)u = κ; r = Z + c_0, and r = Z − σ gives c_0 = −σ.
  The rider's reading of 204 — "a height and a print residue, and nothing more" — is exact
  (line 205's `B_t := 0 if c_t = 0` clause is vacuous here since r(0) ≠ 0 forces σ ≠ 0).

  Carrier side. S1.4 (LIFT), lines 350–366: deg L_k(c) < D; for c ≠ 0, h(L_k(c)) = k and
  dig(L_k(c)) = c. So deg(−L_κ(ση^{q(κ)})) < D = D′ and h = κ, i.e. dv(B_0) = κ. ✓
  Print residue. (HE6-SEAM), S1.2 line 245: res(A(ξ)/ϖ(ξ)^k) = ι_ξ(γ_k(A))·η_ξ^{−q(k)}. At ξ = θ,
  ι_θ = id (r9(a)'s derivation, unchanged by the rider), and (GAMMA) (S1.2, 222–228) is additive in
  the coefficient array, so γ_κ(−L_κ(ση^{q(κ)})) = −ση^{q(κ)} and the print residue is
  −ση^{q(κ)}·η^{−q(κ)} = −σ = c_0. ✓  All three conditions of line 204 are met. CLAIM A1 HOLDS.
  (One scope wrinkle in the same paragraph is booked as minor m-1 below.)

CLAIM A2 — two (LIFT)-permitted choices differ by height > κ.

  Both permitted B_0, B_0′ have dv = κ so dv(E) ≥ κ for E = B_0 − B_0′, deg E < D′.
  Equal print residues + one and the same conversion factor η^{−q(κ)} (an element of K^×, so
  cancellable) give γ_κ(B_0) = γ_κ(B_0′); (GAMMA) additive at fixed height gives γ_κ(E) = 0.
  If h(E) = κ then dig(E) = γ_κ(E) = 0, contradicting S1.2's "dig(A) ∈ K^×" for A ≠ 0 (line 175).
  Hence E = 0 or h(E) > κ. CLAIM A2 HOLDS, exactly as the rider states it.
  Cross-check: this is the same argument the r9(b) SECOND rider runs at Λ vs L_λ(s) (line 3739,
  `grep -cF` over 1..3805 → 1); the two are consistent, and the rider's "restates that closure at
  the display rather than adding to it" is accurate.

