## SECTION (d) — FREE HOSTILE ROUTE: what the pin apparatus actually covers at LEVEL ONE
================================================================================

The surface I chose is the one six passes have audited from the inside — the pin gate's
*containment* claims — but from the opposite direction: not "does every pin resolve?" (it does) but
"does every hypothesis the level-one records claim to discharge have a pinned supplier that actually
contains it?" That is r4 repair 13's standing check, and the answer is no.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
G-1 (GAP) — the level-one records route `(ACCOUNT)` and the S1.7 test assertions to HE6 units that
lie inside NO span of `(PINS)`, and both records assert that the HE6 pins contain them.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The two effective-text sentences, quoted verbatim.

  S3.2, line 889 (base text; not amended by any of r1–r9 or the rider — `grep -nF 'ξ-side'` over the
  whole file returns only 563 and 889):

  > It is monic and is not assumed irreducible. HE6’s ξ-side, evaluation formulas, slope count,
  > resultant argument, and equivariance supply the test assertions and `(ACCOUNT)`.

  S3.1 as r1 repair 2 replaced it, line 1454 (effective; r5 repair 6 amends only the pin LIST on
  that paragraph's first line, not this sentence):

  > For every side denominator \(e'\) and every monic irreducible residual factor \(r'\), the HE6
  > pins supply the monic test polynomial … together with its intended-disk and label properties,
  > generic and raised evaluation values, resultant nonemptiness, disjointness and exhaustion,
  > Galois equivariance, local divisibility, integrality, and the quantitative identity `(ACCOUNT)`.

  And line 1444, which makes the routing exclusive:

  > The HE3 pins supply the base carrier, exact slots, legal full-height lifts, full development,
  > hull/window/cap data, and label equivariance. They are not credited with the master’s universal
  > test package or with `(ACCOUNT)`.

The five HE6 pins, as this pass resolved them, are HE6-PEEL-CONVENTION [83,97], HE6-LIFT-1L
[130,199], HE6-FAMILY [201,213], HE6-SLOT-SEAM [215,238], HE6-PROOF [639,666]. The named suppliers
are HE6's §S3.3 LEMMA HE6-1 "(the ξ-side)" [426,486], §S4 "LEMMA HE6-2 AND HE6-2′ (the two
evaluation displays)" [487,524], §S5 "LEMMA HE6-3 (slope counts, (SEP)-free) AND LEMMA HE6-4
(nonemptiness)" [525,607], and §S6.1 "LEMMA HE6-5 (Galois equivariance …)" [610,638]. Every one of
those four ranges is disjoint from every one of the five pin spans.

Sharpest instance: `(ACCOUNT)`.

  (ACCOUNT) is S1.7's boxed identity Σ_ρ min(w_ρ,κ) = D Σ_λ L_λ min(λ,κ) (line 560), and S1.7 says
  of it: "This is the only side-accounting identity used by the master proof." Its HE6 proof is the
  resultant-symmetry identity

    HE6_PROOF_2026-08-08.md:529  `    (RES)   Σ_{ρ : f(ρ)=0} dv(g(ρ)) = e₁·v(±Res(f,g)) = Σ_{ξ : g(ξ)=0} dv(f(ξ)),`

  and the ξ-side / ρ-side evaluation of it inside LEMMA HE6-3's proof at §S5 — 110 lines before the
  HE6-PROOF span begins. The HE6-PROOF span [639,666] I read in full: it derives |S_{λ,r}| = D′ℓd_r
  and e(g_r) = e₁ℓ, f(g_r) = f₁d_r, and says nothing whatever about Σ_ρ min(w_ρ,κ). Nor does
  THEOREM HE6.A's statement display (HE6:289–300), which in any case is itself pinned by nothing —
  note the asymmetry with HE3, whose statement display IS pinned, as HE3-A-STMT.

  So: the only side-accounting identity the master proof uses has, at both level-one instance
  records, no pinned supplier at all.

Why this is a GAP by the note's own rules, not a matter of taste.
  • S0.2 as restored by r4 repair 8: "No unpinned source material is used to manufacture a theorem
    hypothesis." (ACCOUNT) and the S1.7 test assertions are carrier hypotheses of HE7.A — S4.1 line
    1167 says so in terms: "The theorem assumes the explicit quantitative consequences `(ACCOUNT)`,
    `(RES-DEG)`, nonemptiness, exhaustion … These are source obligations, not conclusions obtained
    merely by naming a carrier."
  • S5 ledger item 3 (line 1194): "Every cited source unit has a named paired begin/end pin." False
    of HE6 §S3.3, §S4, §S5, §S6.1, each cited by description at 889 and at 1454.
  • S1.7's own closing sentence (line 563): "An instance may prove it using generic tests, the ξ- and
    ρ-side evaluations, and resultant symmetry, but those arguments remain inside that instance’s
    pinned proof." At the HE6 instance they demonstrably do not: the instance's pinned proof is
    [639,666] and the ξ-/ρ-side evaluations and resultant symmetry are at [487,607].
  • The standing S7 check (r4 repair 13): "A consumption outside every span fails the gate."
  • The repair shape is one the note has already performed twice, for exactly this reason: r4 repair
    5 re-derived HE3-DEF1 because "the master consumes the construction … [which] is a separate
    bolded unit immediately following DEFINITION 1 and outside the blockquote"; r5 repair 1 pinned
    HETOW-KEY-BRIDGE because "S3.4's own text names LEMMA HETOW-2 by name". Line 889 names five HE6
    units by description and credits them with master hypotheses; line 1454 names them again as
    "the HE6 pins".

Why it is a GAP and not a CRITICAL. Nothing mathematically false is asserted about HE6: §S5 does
prove the accounting identity, and the master's argument from (ACCOUNT) onward is untouched. What
fails is the coverage apparatus and one containment claim about it — precisely the r5 G-1 shape,
which that round's own diagnosis phrased as "The conclusion survives; the stated route does not",
and which was graded GAP. Same grade here.

Scope note (not itself a finding): the r5 repair 4 sweep at line 2802 enumerates six residues
(HETOW-3, GENTOW-4.1, HE7-13, DEFINITION HE6-1, GENHN-3(a), HE3's [r1-N1]) and none of the four HE6
units above. The sweep is the thing the gate re-runs; re-running it is what produced this.

