  > the direction S1.8C consumes.

  "Full" is S1.4's predicate: "k is full ⟺ k ≥ (i(k)+e₁(f₁−1))h, and k ≥ (D′−1)h is uniformly
  sufficient" (lines 389–394). DEFINITION HE6-1's standing hypothesis is HE6:202, "terms with
  κ > D′h". Those differ on (D′−1)h ≤ κ ≤ D′h — a band this note and its source both single out
  (S1.4's two thresholds; HE6-LIFT-1L's sub-threshold set T(k), pinned at r5 repair 4 precisely for
  that). At such a κ the recentering is NOT a family member, so the covering claim is false there.
  The permittedness computation the sentence leans on ("by the permittedness just checked") verifies
  the three conditions of HE6:204 and does not verify HE6:202's κ > D′h.

  Nothing downstream breaks: (WINDOW) (S1.5 line 449) puts every side slope strictly above T = D′h,
  and r9 repair 1(a) already carries "the recipe's standing \(\kappa>D'h=T\)" at the same site, so
  every recentering the master actually forms is at κ > D′h and the covering direction is exact
  there. The defect is one qualifier too wide in a sentence introduced by this rider — hence minor,
  and hence reportable rather than ignorable, since the rider's whole content is one qualifier.

